# Help: SRP initiator and target over soft RDMA
#
# The SCSI RDMA Protocol pair: the ib_srp initiator and the ib_srpt
# LIO fabric target, with the InfiniBand userland interfaces
# (ib_umad, ib_uverbs via USER_ACCESS elsewhere), IPoIB, and the
# device-handler set multipath failover drives (alua, emc, rdac).
# blktests' srp group builds its own LIO target over a soft-RDMA
# link (siw or rxe) and exercises dm-multipath failover across it;
# DM_UEVENT supplies the uevents multipathd reacts to.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - INFINIBAND=m + INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS=y carry the RDMA core and
#   rdma_cm.
# - TARGET_CORE=m gates ib_srpt (an LIO fabric module).
# - SCSI_DH=y gates the device handlers.
#
# Layer builtin/storage/srp-target.config to build the set in (=y)
# for a no-modprobe boot.
# See: drivers/infiniband/ulp/srp/Kconfig
# See: drivers/infiniband/ulp/srpt/Kconfig
# See: drivers/scsi/device_handler/Kconfig

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_INFINIBAND=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS=y
CONFIG_TARGET_CORE=m
CONFIG_SCSI_DH=y

#
# SRP initiator and target
#
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_SRP=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_SRPT=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_USER_MAD=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_IPOIB=m

#
# Multipath device handlers and uevents
#
CONFIG_SCSI_DH_ALUA=m
CONFIG_SCSI_DH_EMC=m
CONFIG_SCSI_DH_RDAC=m
CONFIG_DM_UEVENT=y
